+The fused fp8 GPU layout can arrive as a non-contiguous HND-shaped view over
+dense NHD storage. For example, the 16-token, four-head, packed-head-size-512
+kernel page is exposed as shape `[NB, 4, 16, 512]`, stride
+`[32768, 512, 2048, 1]`. The tensor is non-contiguous only because the two
+middle dimensions are permuted: every page is dense and `stride(0) == 32768`
+puts pages directly next to each other. The edit regroups these pages with
+`as_strided`, multiplying the page stride by `k` and expanding the token axis.
