+For the built-in `fs_native` connector, `max_capacity_gb` is also a hard write
+admission limit. The connector scans existing `.data` and `.tmp` files on
+startup and atomically reserves bytes across store workers. With an LRU
+`eviction` object, the native connector triggers on projected usage at
+`trigger_watermark` and evicts to `trigger_watermark - eviction_ratio` before
+reserving the new write. Its single mutex protects capacity, LRU metadata,
+in-flight reservations, and reader pins; opened retrieves cannot be evicted.
+Abandoned `.tmp` files are counted and are eligible LRU victims. Other eviction
+policies keep using the shared Python controller.
